        {
          "kind": "Function",
          "canonicalReference": "@ory/react-router!createOryProxyHandler:function(1)",
          "docComment": "/**\n * Creates the handler of a resource route that serves the Ory APIs on the app's origin, so Ory's cookies are first-party in local development and preview deployments. In production, use a custom domain on Ory Network, or your own domain with Ory Enterprise License.\n *\n * Reads `ORY_SDK_URL`, and `ORY_PROJECT_API_TOKEN` to sign the base URL rewrite for origins in `trustedOrigins`.\n *\n * Creating the handler registers the proxy for the whole process: the flow helpers and `getOryBaseUrl` then use the request's origin for origins in `trustedOrigins`. A process has one proxy configuration, so call it only in the proxy route module.\n *\n * @param options - The proxy configuration. `trustedOrigins` is required.\n *\n * @example\n * ```ts title=\"app/routes/ory-proxy.ts\"\n * import { createOryProxyHandler } from \"@ory/react-router/proxy\"\n * import config from \"../ory.config\"\n *\n * const proxy = createOryProxyHandler({\n *   ...config,\n *   trustedOrigins: [\"http://localhost:5173\"],\n * })\n *\n * export const loader = proxy\n * export const action = proxy\n * ```\n *\n * @public\n */\n",
