        {
          "kind": "Function",
          "canonicalReference": "@ory/react-router!getOryBaseUrl:function(1)",
          "docComment": "/**\n * Returns the URL the browser uses to reach Ory for this request. The flow, logout, and error helpers use the same URL and attach it to the flows and errors they return, where the Ory Elements components read it. Return it from the loader and pass it as `baseUrl` to `SessionProvider`.\n *\n * The URL is the request's origin only when the app registers the proxy route from `@ory/react-router/proxy` and the origin is in its `trustedOrigins`. Otherwise it is `ORY_SDK_URL`, and a warning with the fix is logged once when that cannot work.\n *\n * @param request - The `request` passed to the loader.\n *\n * @returns The browser URL.\n *\n * @example\n * ```tsx\n * import { SessionProvider } from \"@ory/elements-react/client\"\n * import { Settings } from \"@ory/elements-react/theme\"\n * import { getOryBaseUrl, getSettingsFlow } from \"@ory/react-router\"\n * import type { Route } from \"./+types/settings\"\n * import config from \"../ory.config\"\n *\n * export async function loader({ request }: Route.LoaderArgs) {\n *   return {\n *     flow: await getSettingsFlow(request, config),\n *     baseUrl: getOryBaseUrl(request),\n *   }\n * }\n *\n * export default function SettingsPage({ loaderData }: Route.ComponentProps) {\n *   return (\n *     <SessionProvider baseUrl={loaderData.baseUrl}>\n *       <Settings flow={loaderData.flow} config={config} />\n *     </SessionProvider>\n *   )\n * }\n * ```\n *\n * @public\n */\n",
